1316	// Biases db. For the 8 transformer linears + head: db = Σ_K dY (per output row).
1317	// For patch_proj.bias: db[o] = Σ_{patch rows} dh0[token row, o]. Single owner per
1318	// output element → no atomics.
1319	// PERF FIX (structural, parity-preserved — gated by the K-scaled grad tol, which is
1320	// designed for fp32 accumulation-order differences at large K):
1321	//   (1) The ORIGINAL ran the FULL Σ_K (K up to T=278528) for EVERY bias element on
1322	//       EVERY CTA (no cta/nCTA guard) — 132× redundant work, the dominant cost of P2
1323	//       grad-assembly (measured 59.5% of the step). Columns are now PARTITIONED across
1324	//       CTAs (each global bias column owned by one CTA), removing the 132× redundancy.
1325	//   (2) The K-reduction per column was SERIAL on ONE thread (≈278528 iters). It is now
1326	//       WARP-PARALLEL: a WARP (32 lanes) co-reduces one column — each lane sums a
1327	//       strided 1/32 slice of K (ascending within the lane), then a shuffle tree sums
1328	//       the 32 lane-partials. 32× parallelism per column. The lane reads dY[k*Nout+o]
1329	//       at fixed o with k = lane, lane+32, … (stride 32·Nout); writes by lane 0 only.

